response:
\noindent\textbf{Answer}: the Boeing 707
\end{minipage}

\end{itemize}

\section{Experimental setup}

\subsection{Data}

We use data from a real online reading comprehension system to train our models and collect human evaluations for our experiments. This data has been annotated by expert graders. Specifically, we collected around $1,000$ samples from our online system using the following procedure.

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Input:} The president is also the military commander in chief.
\item \textbf{Gold:} The president is also the military commander.
\item \textbf{Sample Output:} The president is also the military commander.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Factual Question Answering}

\paragraph{Problem:} Given an unanswerable question, generate a factually correct response that is supported by some of the evidence in the input passage.

This data is used to train the Deep Q-network agent. We use a convolutional neural network to provide an estimate of the Q-function. Our network structure is shown in Table \ref{table:neural_network}. Our training environment is a reinforcement learning agent based on a Pytorch implementation of Q-learning.\cite{torch_implementation}

