\subsection{Sentence Boundary Detection}
\label{subsec:sbd}
Given a sentence in a given language, the model must provide the sentence boundary as `.','?','!' in the given language.

\subsection{Part-of-speech Tagging}
\label{subsec:pos}
Given a sentence in a given language, the model must provide the POS tags for all the words in the sentence in the given language as output. For the task, the POS tags have to be chosen from the following list: \url{https://universaldependencies.

\section{Experiments}

\subsection{Experimental Setup}

The model was trained with Adam optimizer \cite{kingma2014adam} using a batch size of 32 samples. The models were trained for 50 epochs, and for evaluation, each model was used to generate output on 1,000 test samples from the test set.

The word embedding size was 256. The convolutional layers used 64 filters of size 3, and 2 convolutional layers each. The fully connected layer had 64 neurons.

